<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Deiotarus Philadelphus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 6 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deiotarus">Deiotarus</a> Philadelphus was the last king of Paphlagonia, a Roman client ruler in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. A son of Castor of Galatia and grandson of Deiotarus, he received Paphlagonia from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a> and kept it under Augustus. On his death in 6 BCE his kingdom was annexed to the Roman province of Galatia.</p></div>
